msgid "NPU高性能编程指南"
msgstr "NPU High-Performance Programming Guide"

msgid "合并Grid分核"
msgstr "Merging Grid split cores"

msgid "一、自动合并Grid分核优化原则"
msgstr "1\\. Principles for Optimizing Automatic Grid Merging and Core Splitting"

msgid "部分场景需要将 Triton 算子从 GPU 迁移到 NPU。由于体系结构差异，基于 GPU 开发的 Triton 算子通常具有较大的逻辑 grid，无法在 NPU 上一次全部调度。昇腾后端会自动把符合条件且逻辑核相互独立的任务映射到可用物理核，并根据 IR 安全分析跳过不适用的 kernel。性能调优时应先检查 grid 大小和编译告警；如果自动 mapping 被跳过，需要通过显式 tiling 或内层循环减小逻辑 grid。"
msgstr "In some scenarios, you need to migrate Triton operators from the GPU to the NPU. Due to architectural differences, Triton operators developed for the GPU usually have a large logical grid. They cannot be fully scheduled on the NPU at one time. The Ascend backend automatically maps eligible tasks with mutually independent logical cores to available physical cores, and skips inapplicable kernels based on IR safety analysis. During performance tuning, first check the grid size and compilation warnings. If automatic mapping is skipped, reduce the logical grid through explicit tiling or inner loops."

msgid "指令并行优化"
msgstr "Instruction-level parallelism optimization"

msgid "一、指令并行优化核心原则"
msgstr "Core Principles of Instruction-Level Parallelism Optimization"

msgid "Triton算子在NPU上执行时，为了提升性能，NPU底层提供multi buffer、指令并行等并行机制，将“数据搬入/数据计算/数据搬出”并行起来，以此来提升性能；但是某些场景下存在multi buffer无法使能问题，影响并行度，导致算子执行性能降低；在性能优化过程中，存在此类问题时，可以参考以下几点做排查，并按照代码示例优化： 1、数据搬运和计算存在数据依赖，产生同步，必须依赖Vector运算后，才能触发MTE搬运，导致并行度低； 2、算子内，无多个数据加载或者单次执行完成无Tiling切分，该场景下无法使能multi buffer； 3、multi buffer需要额外增加UB空间的使用，计算过程中UB空间不足，无法使能multi buffer；"
msgstr "When Triton operators run on the NPU, the underlying NPU provides parallel mechanisms such as multi buffer and instruction parallelism to improve performance. These mechanisms parallelize \"data load / data compute / data store\" to enhance performance. However, in some scenarios, multi buffer cannot be enabled, which affects the degree of parallelism and reduces operator execution performance. During performance tuning, if you encounter such issues, refer to the following points for troubleshooting and optimize according to the code examples: 1. Data movement and computation have data dependencies, causing synchronization. MTE movement can only be triggered after Vector computation is complete, resulting in low parallelism; 2. Within the operator, there are no multiple data loads or no tiling after a single execution. In this scenario, multi buffer cannot be enabled; 3. Multi buffer requires additional UB space. If the UB space is insufficient during computation, multi buffer cannot be enabled;"

msgid "二、代码示例"
msgstr "2\\. Code Examples"

msgid "示例1：减少同步，提升并行度"
msgstr "Example 1: Reduce synchronization to improve parallelism."

msgid "在算子调优过程中，增加指令并行度是算子调优的重要手段。在如下的tl.load语句中，当N > M时, load加载的数据只能填充部分data指向的tensor内存空间中，剩下未填充的部分，如果用户未指定other值，则GPU默认填充为0，为了减少用户迁移的适配工作，NPU保持行为和GPU一致。NPU会先用Vector核将data指向的全部内存空间设置为指定值(如果用户未指定other值，同样设置为0)，然后再使用MTE2指令搬运数据到data指向的部分内存空间，这样就会导致MTE2和Vector产生依赖，无法高效并行，影响性能："
msgstr "During operator tuning, increasing instruction parallelism is an important method. In the following tl.load statement, when N > M, the loaded data fills only part of the tensor memory space pointed to by data. For the remaining unfilled part, if you do not specify the other value, the GPU fills it with 0 by default. To reduce the adaptation work during migration, the NPU maintains the same behavior as the GPU. The NPU first uses the Vector core to set the entire memory space pointed to by data to the specified value. If you do not specify the other value, the NPU sets the space to 0. Then, it uses the MTE2 instruction to move the data to the part of the memory space pointed to by data. This creates a dependency between the MTE2 and Vector cores, preventing efficient parallel execution and affecting performance:"

msgid "为了提升性能，在load加载数据只能部分填充到指向的内存空间时，如果未填充的部分不影响后续的计算结果，可以在load语句中，添加care_padding=False来去掉默认值的填充，增加并行度，提升性能，上面算子的优化写法如下："
msgstr "To improve performance, if the data loaded by load only partially fills the targeted memory space, check whether the unfilled part affects subsequent computation results. If it does not, add care_padding=False to the load statement to remove default value padding, increase parallelism, and improve performance. The optimized way to write the preceding operator is as follows:"

msgid "示例2：在Triton算子内，使用for循环，增加Tiling，提升并行度"
msgstr "Example 2: Inside a Triton operator, use a for loop to add Tiling and improve parallelism."

msgid "在Triton算子编程中，mask运算经常运用在load/store/where等语法中，在性能优化过程中，需要特别注意这类运算导致的性能下降。当Triton算子内逻辑是单次顺序执行，开始->数据搬入->计算->数据搬出->结束，指令无法并行，执行效率低;可以通过在算子使用for循环增加tiling，将单次处理量减少，多次处理，能够让\"数据搬入/计算/数据搬出\"并行起来，减少串行的等待时间，提升整体性能；同时使用for循环增加Tiling，也能降低单次处理消耗的UB空间。   需要注意：增加数据Tiling也同时需要考虑改变数据切块后的数学是否等价。"
msgstr "In Triton operator programming, mask operations are frequently used in syntaxes such as load, store, and where. During performance tuning, pay special attention to the performance degradation caused by these operations. If a Triton operator executes sequentially in a single pass (start -> data movement in -> computation -> data movement out -> end), instructions cannot run in parallel, resulting in low execution efficiency. You can use a for loop in the operator to add tiling, reducing the processing volume per pass and processing data in multiple passes. This allows \"data movement in/computation/data movement out\" to run in parallel, reducing serial wait time and improving overall performance. At the same time, using a for loop to add tiling also reduces the UB space consumed per pass.   Note: When adding data tiling, you must also consider whether the mathematics remain equivalent after changing the data blocking."

msgid "数据类型优化"
msgstr "Data type optimization"

msgid "一、数据类型优化核心原则"
msgstr "1\\. Core Principles of Data Type Optimization"

msgid "Atlas A2系列产品、Atlas A3系列产品 向量运算单元的部分运算操作不支持某些数据类型，这种场景下，对应的向量运算会退化为标量运算，影响性能。在确定不影响整体算子精度的情况下，建议使用支持的数据类型，提升性能。 主要涉及以下操作"
msgstr "For Atlas A2 series products and Atlas A3 series products, some operations of the vector computing unit do not support certain data types. In this scenario, the corresponding vector operations degrade to scalar operations, which affects performance. When you confirm that the overall operator precision is not affected, use supported data types to improve performance. This mainly involves the following operations:"

msgid "**OP名称**"
msgstr "**OP Name**"

msgid "**不支持的数据类型**"
msgstr "**Unsupported Data Types**"

msgid "Vector ADD"
msgstr "Vector ADD"

msgid "int64"
msgstr "int64"

msgid "Vector CMP"
msgstr "Vector CMP"

msgid "int64/int32"
msgstr "int64/int32"

msgid "Vector Add Triton算子示例代码"
msgstr "Vector Add Triton operator example code"

msgid "如下Triton算子，当x, y input tensor使用的数据类型是int64时，会导致x1+y1运算展开为Scalar运算，降低性能，在不影响精度的情况下，建议使用int32数据类型。"
msgstr "For the following Triton operator, when the data type of the x and y input tensors is int64, the x1+y1 operation is expanded into scalar operations, reducing performance. If precision is not affected, use the int32 data type."

msgid "Vector Cmp Triton算子示例代码"
msgstr "Vector Cmp Triton operator sample code"

msgid "如下Triton算子，做mask运算时，使用到了Cmp操作，Cmp不支持int64/int32数据类型，会导致cols < N运算展开为Scalar运算，降低性能，在不影响精度的情况下，建议使用fp32数据类型。   在Triton算子编程中，mask运算经常运用在load/store/where等语法中，在性能优化过程中，需要特别注意这类运算导致的性能下降。"
msgstr "In the following Triton operator, the Cmp operation is used for mask operations. Cmp does not support int64/int32 data types. This causes the cols < N operation to be expanded into scalar operations, reducing performance. If precision is not affected, use the fp32 data type.   In Triton operator programming, mask operations are frequently used in syntaxes such as load, store, and where. During performance optimization, pay special attention to the performance degradation caused by these operations."